From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Settings > About, the computer's name

ChromiumOS has no computer name: every NickelOS computer was "localhost"
in the Terminal and to Linux apps, and Settings had no way to change it
(ChromeOS's own "Device name" setting is gone; only an enterprise policy
names devices now).

This adds a Computer name row to the About page, under the update rows,
with a Change button and dialog. The name is kept as typed ("Dresden's
Laptop"); nickel-hostnamed (org.freedesktop.hostname1, as on other
distributions) makes the hostname from it ("Dresdens-Laptop"), which the
row shows too when it reads differently. Changes are for administrators of
the computer; nickel-hostnamed checks, and the row says so to everyone
else. A name with no letter or digit a hostname can hold (one written only
in another script) gets an error in the dialog.

NickelComputerNameHandler reads the hostname1 properties and calls
org.nickelos.Hostname1's CanChange and SetName.

The strings are in ui_chromeos_strings.grd, which few files include.

